# Workforce env file for LOCAL development. Copy it, then fill in your key:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` and `.env.local` stay LOCAL: they are gitignored and must never be
# committed. Values already exported in your shell always win over env files.
# The API loads, highest precedence first: apps/api/.env.local > .env.local
# (repo root) > apps/api/.env > .env (repo root) — see apps/api/README.md.
#
# The key is read only by the API server process; the browser app needs none.
# It is never logged. Put YOUR OWN personal key below:
OLLAMA_API_KEY=replace_with_your_personal_key

# Optional overrides (keep entries filled — a bare `KEY=` empty value fails
# config validation once loaded). Defaults live in apps/api/README.md:
# OLLAMA_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=https://ollama.com/v1
# REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://workforce:workforce@127.0.0.1:55432/workforce
# EMBEDDING_CACHE_DIR=.cache/workforce-models
# PORT=3001
# WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# ---- Phase 6 Docker production stack (`docker compose up --build`) ---------
# The stack reads configuration from the environment or THIS root `.env`
# (compose auto-loads it; values already exported in your shell win).
# Same required values as `npm run dev`: OLLAMA_API_KEY, BETTER_AUTH_SECRET,
# BETTER_AUTH_URL, DELEGATION_CONTEXT_SECRET and one complete OAuth pair
# (GOOGLE_* and/or GITHUB_*). Omissions fail API startup with safe errors.
#
# Host ports are env-overridable (defaults below); the DB/Redis ports stay
# published on 127.0.0.1 only:
#   WEB_HOST_PORT=3000
#   API_HOST_PORT=3001
# If you change them, keep the browser-facing URLs coherent:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001   (public, non-secret, build arg)
#   BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3001
#   WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
#
# Inside the compose network the containers always use the internal
# hostnames (postgres:5432 / redis:6379). A dev DATABASE_URL/REDIS_URL with
# 127.0.0.1 ports in this file is IGNORED by the stack; override the internal
# topology only for external managed stores:
#   WORKFORCE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...
#   WORKFORCE_REDIS_URL=redis://...
# The scheduler worker receives ONLY REDIS_URL, INTERNAL_API_BASE_URL,
# DELEGATION_CONTEXT_SECRET and optional queue/timeout values.
# No secret is ever baked into images or build args.
#
# ---- Phase 6 SINGLE-ORIGIN PROXY MODE (web /api rewrite, build + runtime) --
# WORKFORCE_WEB_INTERNAL_API_URL drives the web container's API_INTERNAL_URL
# in TWO roles: (1) BUILD-TIME Next rewrite target — the web build reads it
# and next.config.ts bakes /api/:path* -> <target> into the standalone routes
# manifest — and (2) RUNTIME SSR base — the same env value is injected into
# the container and `resolveServerApiBaseUrl` uses it for server-side chat
# hydration (absent/blank at runtime falls back to NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL).
# Changing role (1) requires a rebuild (`docker compose up --build`);
# role (2) follows the container's runtime env. Compose default:
# http://api:3001 (API stays private; single-origin proxy mode). Never a
# secret (bounded http(s) origin, no path/query/credentials).
#
# DISTINCT from WORKFORCE_INTERNAL_API_URL (see the api/scheduler sections):
# that one is the RUNTIME same-REST base for the API's own tool/delegation
# calls (API default loopback http://127.0.0.1:3001) and for the scheduler's
# calls to the API (scheduler default http://api:3001). Never set
# WORKFORCE_INTERNAL_API_URL to a web-side URL inside Compose — the
# scheduler would call itself.
#
# ---- Railway production only (docs/deployment/railway.md) ------------------
# Deployed topology keeps the API PRIVATE: web is the ONLY public origin.
